      "writtenOn": "2021-01-19T23:14:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "subId match here will actually allow \"dangling\" requests if the subId changes for a given phone object but only if those subIds were previously active. Since there will always only be one active subId for a phone, and since we\u0027re only intending to let the requests live on active subscriptions, I think we need to:\n1) clear the list when the phone\u0027s active subId changes, and possibly:\n2) not bother checking for a subId match here (depends on how the clear()) is implemented).\n\nOtherwise, we\u0027re just changing the race condition under which requests can succeed. I need to think a little more about this.",
      "range": {
